ividually by Admin after signup; no third-party verification.\\\\n- One household account per email; additional household members may have separate resident users if desired.\\\\n- Custom domain will be connected (e.g., YourHOA.org).\\\\n\\\\nSuccess Criteria (MVP)\\\\n- Admin can publish a post with an image and attachment in under 5 minutes using a visual editor.\\\\n- Residents can sign in and reach member-only content within 2 clicks from the homepage.\\\\n- 80% of active residents onboarded within 30 days of launch.\\\\n- Routine updates require zero custom code.\\\\n\\\\nTimeline & Launch Checklist\\\\n- Week 1: Choose template, set branding, create pages, configure members area and roles, set up contact form, import legal docs, write first 3 News posts, prepare onboarding email.\\\\n- Week 2: Test signup/approval flow, invite pilot residents, fix content gaps, connect domain, go live, announce to community.\\\\n\\\\nAcceptance Tests\\\\n- Admin uploads a PDF to Legal Docs; it appears under the correct category without code.\\\\n- New resident signs up; admin approves; resident can view Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events.\\\\n- Admin publishes a News post with one image and one attached PDF; it appears in member section and optional teaser on Home.\\\\n- Contact form submission delivers to the HOA email and shows an on-page confirmation.\\\\n\\\\nFuture Enhancements (Post-MVP)\\\\n- Online dues payments with receipts and payment history (Stripe/PayPal or platform integrations).\\\\n- Opt-in resident directory with privacy controls.\\\\n- Maintenance/work order request form with status tracking.\\\\n- Email newsletter (auto-email new posts).\\\\n- Event RSVPs with calendar invites.\\\\n- Multi-language support and accessibility audit.\\\\n\\\\nNon-Goals (MVP)\\\\n- Custom-built backend, custom code, or complex integrations.\\\\n- Advanced CRM or accounting within the site.\\\\n- Complex resident verification beyond admin approval.\\\\n\\\\nRationale\\\\n- The solution is achievable with current no-code platforms, aligns with a non-technical admin’s needs, and keeps sensitive operations (payments, advanced verification) out of MVP to minimize risk and complexity.\\\"\\n}\\n###STORE-001-HOA-WISH###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":3727,\"outputTokens\":3752,\"totalTokens\":7479},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-C77h15bo4LZ2e0vg0yniXJo42ujxc\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1755813903,\"model\":\"gpt-5-2025-08-07\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###STORE-001-HOA-WISH###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"USER WISH: HOA Info Hub (Simple Website with Resident-Only Sections)\\\\n\\\\nPersona\\\\n- Primary Admin: HOA board member or volunteer with little to no technical background. Needs to publish updates, upload documents, approve residents, and respond to inquiries without coding.\\\\n- Residents: Community members who need easy access to dues info, meeting details, and announcements after signing in.\\\\n- Prospective Residents: People researching the neighborhood who need public info and documents.\\\\n\\\\nGoals\\\\n- Provide a simple, user-friendly website for HOA information access.\\\\n- Offer resident-only pages for Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events.\\\\n- Enable non-technical admins to update content (blog/updates) without coding.\\\\n- Include a Contact Us form that routes to an HOA email with basic spam protection.\\\\n\\\\nMVP Scope\\\\n1) Public Pages\\\\n- Home: Brief HOA intro; quick links to Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us.\\\\n- Legal Docs: Upload and list PDFs (CC&Rs, bylaws, policies). Categories and title search.\\\\n- Schools: Curated links and brief descriptions of nearby schools; easily editable.\\\\n- Contact Us: Form (name, email, subject, message; optional topic dropdown). Sends to HOA inbox with success confirmation.\\\\n\\\\n2) Resident-Only Pages (Sign-in required)\\\\n- Dues: Informational page with dues schedule, amounts, and how to pay; optional external payment link. Downloadable PDFs.\\\\n- Annual Meetings: List/calendar of upcoming meetings with details; agenda PDFs and past minutes as downloads; optional RSVP toggle.\\\\n- News & Events: Blog-style updates with categories (News, Events, Notices), inline images, and attachments. Optional homepage teaser of latest 3 posts.\\\\n\\\\n3) Authentication and Access Control\\\\n- Member signup with email and password or magic link; admin approval required before access.\\\\n- Collected fields: name, email, street address (used by admin to verify residency).\\\\n- Roles:\\\\n  - Admin: Full control of settings, member approvals, content, and documents.\\\\n  - Editor: Can create and publish content and events; cannot change settings or approve members.\\\\n  - Resident: Read-only access to member-only pages.\\\\n\\\\n4) Content Management (No-Code)\\\\n- Visual WYSIWYG editor (headings, images, lists, links, attachments).\\\\n- Drag-and-drop uploads for PDFs and images with automatic file library.\\\\n- Prebuilt templates for Legal Docs and News posts.\\\\n- Simple navigation manager to reorder/add menu items.\\\\n- Draft previews and scheduled publishing.\\\\n\\\\n5) Contact Form\\\\n- Sends to designated HOA email address.\\\\n- Basic spam protection (captcha or platform equivalent).\\\\n- Optional auto-reply acknowledgment.\\\\n- Submissions viewable in an admin inbox on the platform.\\\\n\\\\n6) Design & UX\\\\n- Clean, mobile-responsive template with readable fonts and good contrast.\\\\n- Simple top navigation: Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us, plus a Member Login/Portal link. After login, member pages appear in nav.\\\\n- Site search (page/post titles at minimum).\\\\n- Easy branding updates (logo, colors) without code.\\\\n\\\\n7) Privacy & Security\\\\n- SSL enabled by default.\\\\n- Minimal personal data stored (name, email, address). No financial data in MVP.\\\\n- Admin can