uture Enhancements (Post-MVP)\\\\n- Online dues payments with receipts and payment history (Stripe/PayPal or platform integrations).\\\\n- Opt-in resident directory with privacy controls.\\\\n- Maintenance/work order request form with status tracking.\\\\n- Email newsletter (auto-email new posts).\\\\n- Event RSVPs with calendar invites.\\\\n- Multi-language support and accessibility audit.\\\\n\\\\nNon-Goals (MVP)\\\\n- Custom-built backend, custom code, or complex integrations.\\\\n- Advanced CRM or accounting within the site.\\\\n- Complex resident verification beyond admin approval.\\\\n\\\\nRationale\\\\n- The solution is achievable with current no-code platforms, aligns with a non-technical admin’s needs, and keeps sensitive operations (payments, advanced verification) out of MVP to minimize risk and complexity.\\\"\\n}\\n###STORE-001-HOA-WISH###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":3727,\"completion_tokens\":3752,\"total_tokens\":7479,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":2432,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a helpful, friendly AI software development assistant focused on helping users of all technical skill levels transform their app ideas, goals, and stories into a concrete idea for an app.\\n\\nWhether it be an expert developer or a non-technical user, you will be responsible for guiding them through the process of defining their app idea out of nebulous concepts.\\n\\n## 2. A Complete User Wish\\n\\nYour goal is to produce a \\\"user wish\\\". A valid wish meets the following criteria:\\n\\n- Self-Contained: The wish should be a complete, logical app idea that makes sense. For instance, it should not be a collection of unrelated features or a vague concept. It should also be logically sound and not contain contradictions.\\n- Achievable: The wish should be something that can realistically be built with current AI technology and cloud/development resources. It should not be overly ambitious or require impossible features.\\n- Clear: The wish should be clearly defined and understandable, as well as contain clear high-level requirements.\\n- User Background/Persona: The wish should include a brief description of the user or persona who would use the app, including their background, skill level, needs, and goals.\\n\\n## 3. Your Role\\n\\nYou serve as the Chief for the user, meaning you can recruit and assign tasks to autonomous AI agents of your own. However, you are the only one with the ability to interact with the user and submit the finished user wish.\\n\\n## 4. Operational Model\\n\\nYou and your AI subordinate agents do not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses).\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n## 5. List of System Calls\\n\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"GENERATE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Generate\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate an AI response from a prompt. This is useful for brainstorming, writing code, or getting another perspective from a fresh AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Provide prompt in the promptString parameter. The generation will be performed by a temporary, isolated AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"promptString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\",\\n      \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\",\\n      \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit your completed user wish.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"STORE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Store\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"storageString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RETRIEVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"retrievalString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"FORGET\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"forgetString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hello Chief Agent! Initial user responses: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"[object Object]\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###PHASE-001-HOA###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user is a non-technical HOA stakeholder seeking a simple, resident-friendly website with public info and resident-only sections. Their inputs are specific and achievable with current web/CMS tools. This user wish consolidates their goals into a clear, self-contained, and realistic specification with default decisions that minimize complexity while preserving room for growth.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"USER WISH: HOA Info Hub (Simple Website with Resident-Only Sections)\\\\n\\\\nPersona\\\\n- Primary Admin: HOA board member or volunteer with little to no technical background. Needs to publish updates, upload documents, approve residents, and respond to inquiries quickly without coding.\\\\n- Residents: Adults living in the HOA community who need easy access to dues info, meeting details, and announcements after signing in.\\\\n- Prospective Residents: People researching the neighborhood who need public info and documents.\\\\n\\\\nGoals\\\\n- Provide a simple, user-friendly website for easy access to HOA information.\\\\n- Offer resident-only pages for Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events.\\\\n- Enable non-technical admins to update content (blog/updates) without coding.\\\\n- Offer a Contact Us form for questions, routing inquiries to an HOA email.\\\\n\\\\nSuccess Criteria (MVP)\\\\n- Admin can publish a post with images/attachments in under 5 minutes using a visual editor.\\\\n- Residents can sign in and access member-only pages within 2 clicks from the homepage.\\\\n- 80% of active residents onboarded within 30 days of launch.\\\\n- Zero custom code required for routine content updates; uptime comparable to managed website platforms.\\\\n\\\\nScope (MVP Features)\\\\n1) Public Pages\\\\n- Home: Brief HOA intro, quick links to Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us.\\\\n- Legal Docs: Upload and list PDFs (e.g., CC&Rs, bylaws, policies). Supports file categories and search by title.\\\\n- Schools: Curated links and brief descriptions of nearby schools; easily editable by admin.\\\\n- Contact Us: Contact form with name, email, subject, message; optional topic dropdown (General, Dues, Meetings). Form sends to HOA inbox and shows on-page success message.\\\\n\\\\n2) Resident-Only Pages (Sign-in Required)\\\\n- Dues: Informational page with dues schedule, amounts, and how to pay (initially informational only; link out to payment processor if used). Can include downloadable PDFs (statements, schedules).\\\\n- Annual Meetings: Calendar/list of upcoming meetings, location details, agenda PDFs, and past minutes as downloadable PDFs. Optional RSVP toggle for events.\\\\n- News & Events: Blog-style updates with categories (News, Events, Notices). Posts can include inline images and attachments. Latest 3 posts can be optionally previewed on the homepage with teaser text.\\\\n\\\\n3) Authentication and Access Control\\\\n- Member signup page with email and password (or magic link). Default: Admin approval required before a new account can access member-only pages.\\\\n- Account data collected: name, email, street address; admin can verify residency via address match before approval.\\\\n- Roles:\\\\n  - Admin: Full control of settings, member approvals, content, documents.\\\\n  - Editor: Can create and publish content and events, upload files; cannot change settings or approve members.\\\\n  - Resident: Read-only access to member-only pages.\\\\n\\\\n4) Content Management (No-Code)\\\\n- Visual WYSIWYG editor for pages and posts (headings, images, lists, links, attachments).\\\\n- Drag-and-drop file upload for PDFs and images with automatic file library.\\\\n- Prebuilt page templates for Legal Docs and News posts.\\\\n- Simple navigation manager to reorder/add menu items.\\\\n- Scheduled publishing and draft previews.\\\\n\\\\n5) Contact Form\\\\n- Sends submissions to a designated HOA email address.\\\\n- Basic spam protection (captcha or platform equivalent).\\\\n- Optional auto-reply acknowledgment to the sender.\\\\n- Submissions viewable in an admin inbox on the platform.\\\\n\\\\n6) Design & UX\\\\n- Clean, mobile-responsive template with large, readable fonts and clear contrast.\\\\n- Simple top navigation: Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us, plus a Member Login/Portal link. After login, Member pages appear in nav.\\\\n- Site search (at minimum searches page/post titles; platform-provided search acceptable).\\\\n- Placeholder for logo and colors; can be updated by Admin without code.\\\\n\\\\n7) Privacy & Security\\\\n- SSL enabled by default.\\\\n- Store minimal personal data (name, email, address). No sensitive financial data in MVP.\\\\n- Admin can export resident list and delete accounts on request.\\\\n- Platform-managed backups and security patches.\\\\n\\\\nImplementation Approach (Recommended, No-Code)\\\\n- Use a managed website builder with built-in members area, blog, forms, and file library.\\\\n- Example Option A (recommended for simplicity): Squarespace Business + Member Areas (or equivalent). Includes: visual editor, forms, protected pages, basic search, built-in email capture, and analytics.\\\\n- Example Option B: Wix with Members Area and Blog.\\\\n- Either option supports: custom domain, SSL, simple admin/editor roles, and member-only pages with admin approval workflow.\\\\n\\\\nAssumptions (MVP)\\\\n- No online dues payments in MVP (info-only with optional external payment link). Can be added later via native integrations or links.\\\\n- Resident access is granted individually by Admin after signup; no automatic verification against third-party databases.\\\\n- One household account per email; additional household members can be added as separate resident users if desired.\\\\n- Custom domain will be connected (e.g., YourHOA.org).\\\\n\\\\nTimeline & Launch Checklist\\\\n- Week 1: Choose template; set branding basics; create pages; configure members area and roles; set up contact form; import initial legal docs; write first 3 News posts; prepare resident onboarding email.\\\\n- Week 2: Test sign-up/approval flow; invite pilot residents; fix content gaps; connect custom domain; go live; announce to community.\\\\n\\\\nFuture Enhancements (Post-MVP)\\\\n- Online dues payments with receipts and payment history (via Stripe/PayPal or platform integrations).\\\\n- Self-service resident directory with opt-in privacy controls.\\\\n- Work order/maintenance request form with status tracking.\\\\n- Email newsletter from the platform (News post auto-email).\\\\n- Event RSVPs with calendar invites.\\\\n- Multi-language support and accessibility audit.\\\\n\\\\nNon-Goals (MVP)\\\\n- Custom-built backend, custom code, or complex integrations.\\\\n- Advanced CRM or accounting within the site.\\\\n- Complex resident verification beyond admin approval.\\\\n\\\\nAcceptance Tests (Examples)\\\\n- Admin can upload a PDF to Legal Docs and it appears under the correct category without code.\\\\n- New resident signs up; admin approves; resident can view Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events.\\\\n- Admin publishes a News post with one image and one attached PDF; it appears in Member section and optional teaser on Home.\\\\n- Contact form submission delivers to the HOA email and shows confirmation to the user.\\\\n\\\\nThis wish is self-contained, achievable using off-the-shelf website platforms, and optimized for a non-technical admin to operate.\\\"\\n}\\n###PHASE-001-HOA###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID PHASE-001-HOA failed inspection: Call PHASE-001-HOA of type PHASE failed inspection: agent 1 is not the Chief.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1755813901572,"endTime":1755813977719.8237}